<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36649" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plēnĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		plenus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a being full</i>, <i>fulness</i>, <i>repletion</i> (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nubes propter plenitatem et gravitatem
					liquescendo disperguntur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					8, 2, 2</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">5, 9,
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>abundance</i>, <i>copiousness</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">humoris plenitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					6, 1, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
